<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mar Piccolo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mar Piccolo is a shallow inner sea at Taranto in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, linked by narrow channels to the outer bay, the Mar Grande. It gave ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarentum">Taras</a> and later Taranto one of the best harbours of southern Italy and has long been used for shellfish farming. An arsenal of the Italian navy stands on its shore.</p></div>
